# All settings are optional; the defaults work with `docker compose up -d` and the backend running.
# Copy to .env.local to override. Vite exposes every VITE_ variable to the browser, so never put a secret here.

# Currency used to show vehicle prices: an ISO 4217 code such as USD, EUR, GBP or INR.
# VITE_CURRENCY=USD

# Locale used to format numbers and currency (defaults to the browser's language), e.g. en-US, de-DE, en-IN.
# VITE_LOCALE=

# Where the API lives. Leave unset in development: the dev server proxies /api to http://localhost:3000.
# Set it for a production build to the API's full address, e.g. https://car-dealership-api.onrender.com
# (with the scheme, no trailing path). It is baked in at build time, so change it, then redeploy.
# The API must also list this site's address in its CORS_ORIGIN. See ../DEPLOYMENT.md.
# VITE_API_URL=
